    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into tonight\u2019s slate with **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** serving as our primary offensive engine, boasting an elite 74.56 score. Facing Feltner and his 4.98 xERA, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** is positioned perfectly in the cleanup spot to capitalize on a high-ceiling matchup where his platoon dynamics and park factors align for maximum production. **Drake Baldwin** follows closely behind with a 69.17 rating; his lead-off role against Martinez provides a high floor, as the +16% SP skill adjustment highlights a clear tactical advantage for **Drake Baldwin** to set the table early. **Dominic Smith** rounds out the starters with a 58.04 score, serving as our most reliable utility asset today by leveraging the same favorable matchup against Martinez that elevates our catcher\u2019s profile.\n\nThe middle of the lineup remains in a \"wait and see\" pattern, as **Sam Antonacci** (48.61) and **Miguel Vargas** (45.59) face a significantly tougher test against Jones. While **Sam Antonacci** receives a healthy bump for his lead-off duties, both he and **Miguel Vargas** are hampered by Jones\u2019s 3.57 xERA, limiting their upside to marginal category support. **Dominic Smith** was the closest call for the bench today, but his efficiency narrowly outpaced the lower-tier prospects and bench depth, confirming him as the final viable play. With **Kyle Tucker**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, and **Gunnar Henderson** all sidelined by a team off-day, we are effectively running a skeleton crew. We continue to monitor the status of **Luis Robert Jr.**, who remains out on the IL, leaving the burden of production on our active starters to hold the line during this mid-week stretch.",
